-- Compound-guard messages. These runtime checks are typecheck-shadowed for
-- ordinary code; `quote` outputs an unconstrained 'a, so a quoted scalar or
-- tagged binding slips the checker and must die with the exact guard text.
-- EXPECT: len: expected compound, got int
5 'x let 'x quote len

-- EXPECT: len: tagged values have no length (case-match first)
5 ok 'x let 'x quote len

-- EXPECT: push: expected list or tuple, got int
5 'x let 'x quote 1 push

-- EXPECT: push: expected list or tuple, got tagged
5 ok 'x let 'x quote 1 push

-- EXPECT: pop: expected list or tuple, got int
5 'x let 'x quote pop drop

-- EXPECT: pop: expected list or tuple, got tagged
5 ok 'x let 'x quote pop drop

-- EXPECT: get: expected list or tuple, got int
5 'x let 'x quote 0 get drop

-- EXPECT: get: expected list or tuple, got tagged
5 ok 'x let 'x quote 0 get drop

-- EXPECT: set: expected list or tuple, got int
5 'x let 'x quote 0 1 set drop

-- EXPECT: set: expected list or tuple, got tagged
5 ok 'x let 'x quote 0 1 set drop

-- EXPECT: cat: expected compound, got int
5 'x let [] 'x quote cat drop

-- EXPECT: cat: cannot cat tagged values
5 ok 'x let [] 'x quote cat drop

-- a body that pushes literals onto a nearly full operand stack
-- EXPECT: stack overflow
0 2097150 range ((1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8) drop) apply len drop

-- The same ceiling reached through the per-body check in `eval_body` rather than
-- through SPUSH. An inline `(...) apply` cannot reach it: the tuple literal is
-- SPUSHed onto the operand stack before `apply` pops it, so SPUSH fires first.
-- A body reached through a *binding* is never on the operand stack, so the
-- per-body check is the only thing between its literals and the end of `stack`.
-- Verified falsifiable: delete the check and this line succeeds.
-- EXPECT: stack overflow
(1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 drop drop drop drop drop drop drop drop) 'many let 0 2097146 range many len drop

-- Only the SPUSH check catches this one. The per-body check bounds what a body's
-- own literals can add, and a bound name is not a literal: `dispatch_word`
-- SPUSHes the whole binding, so two lookups of a one-million-slot list overrun a
-- stack that the body guard measured as almost empty.
-- EXPECT: stack overflow
0 1048600 range 'big let big big len drop len drop

